regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:1:**VERDICT: the fix as displayed is semantically sound and every detector expectation I could walk checks out — but two of the brief's own meta-premises fail packet-internal audit, and the latch-independence property is defended for only ONE of the twelve other latch sites. §C0 says "2 hunks, 58 changed lines"; the displayed diff has THREE hunk headers, its hunk headers do not match its own bodies (so "verbatim" fails), and 58 reconciles only as *non-blank* insertions+deletions (61 raw − 3 blank added, header-derived). The un-defended cell is real: a one-token edit, `SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12` → `1 << 11`, passes all 14 rows.**
