regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:5:- **P1 (READ).** "2 hunks" is false against the packet's own diff: I count three `@@` headers (`-146,13`, `-306,6`, `-328,16`). The fix cannot compile without the enum hunk, so the real working set has ≥3; "2" is a miscount, carried into PRETABLE as "58 changed lines."
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:6:- **P2 (READ + REASONED).** The hunk headers are mutually consistent (offsets accumulate: 306+14=320, 328+15=343) but **disagree with their own bodies** (hunk 1: header 13/27 vs body 11/20; hunk 2: 6/7 vs 5/6; hunk 3: 16/36 vs 16/35). A verbatim `git diff` cannot do that — the block was re-wrapped, and ~7 lines are unaccounted in the rendering. Under the header-derived counts: 48 insertions + 13 deletions = 61 raw, **58 excluding the three blank added lines** — so "58" is defensible only under that counting; my body count gives 55. Cite neither number as settled.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:7:- **P3 (READ).** Label collision: §S3's "candidate (b)" is the **fix** (skip the store); the detector contract's "(b)" is the **defect** (verbatim arm reinstated); "(d)" is never defined. A seat "confirming (b) is caught" is ambiguous in this packet.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:8:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:9:## Q1
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:10:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:11:- **(a) READ** for the visible region: between the switch's close and `} else {` the hunk shows exactly one statement — the now-guarded `memory_rw`. Visible arms write `buf` only (`buf[0] = *color;`; `buf[2] = *color >> 16; buf[3] = *color >> 24;`). The RGB/RGBA arms sit in the unchanged 16-line gap between hunks 2 and 3; fill-only there is **REASONED** from the accept rows being stably green on HEAD. GET branch: displayed only as context; byte-identical **GIVEN** the diff is the complete change set — the premise §C0 miscounts, so I take completeness from the displayed diff, not from §C0's arithmetic.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:12:- **(b) READ** for the visible path (with `ok==0`: `ok=0`, latch test/set, `fatal(color_mode,x,y)` — nothing reads `buf`; the only visible `buf` reader is skipped). **REASONED** for the unseen tail: if anything after the if/else read `buf` on the PUT path, HEAD's supported PUTs would misbehave, contradicting the stable accept rows. Not fully settleable: the function's lines after the else. PRETABLE's "not observable; SENTENCE" is honest; I add: also not READ-verifiable here.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:13:- **(c) READ**: the *removed* comment itself claimed "THE NEXT FREE BIT IS 1 << 12"; visible neighbours BADMODE=1<<10, TEX_RD=1<<11; BADCOLOR=1<<12 gives 13 distinct bits (coheres with PRETABLE §3). **NOT CHECKABLE**: that nothing else in `dev_sgi_re.c` uses bit 12 of `d->warned` — a stale next-free-bit comment is exactly how collisions happen. Settling fact: grep the file for `1 << 12`/`0x1000`/`4096` and enumerate every `d->warned` use.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:14:- **(d) NOT CHECKABLE**: no other consumer of "color mode =" is inlined. The one inlined consumer (witness `ycrcb attrib`) is satisfied by the retained prefix *as a substring*. Two risks a grep must rule out: end-anchored/exact-line matches (the new line continues past the prefix) and **count-based** probes (per-pixel → per-process changes the count). Also #504's announce text (not inlined) must not contain the ANN substring, or `latch indep` loses discrimination. Settling fact: `grep -rn "color mode" regress/` plus each hit's match style, and #504's fatal string.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:15:- **(e) REASONED, walked**: MODE_CI8=0x1000 → bufdepth = 1<<((0x1000>>8)&3) = 1 (**READ** formula, #100 comment); CI stores buf[0] = 0xdd (**READ** context; fg=0xaabbccdd **READ**); paint 0x11223344, top byte 0x11 → 0xdd = **0xdd223344** ✓. The BE premise is *forced by the packet's own numbers*: `abgr put` is green on HEAD (from 2/5 + 6/14, below) and 0xddccbbaa is derivable from the visible ABGR context lines (dd,cc,bb,aa) **only** under a BE read. Uncheckable: that setup_put's CI8 byte lands on the word's byte 0 (witness half not inlined).
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:16:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:17:## Q2 (REASONED)
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:18:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:19:One token: `1 << 12` → `1 << 11`. C permits duplicate enumerator values; the colour latch now shares **TEX_RD**'s bit, and no session fires TEX_RD (detector sessions are DE PUTs + loads; TEX_RD and the six width latches fire on texture reads, per the enum's own comment). I walked all 14 rows — every one stays green; `announce text`/`two declined`/`once` precede the colour decline with no tex read, and `latch indep` fires only BADMODE (1<<10), which no longer collides. **The row I expect to stay green is `latch indep`** — the row whose entire purpose this edit defeats. It breaks the property the enum comment itself asserts ("a latch shared with **any other site**…"): a guest that reads a texture, then issues a bad-colour PUT, gets no announce at all. **Undisclosed** — the contract rows the latch only against BADMODE. (Precondition, itself uncheckable: the witness half does no texture reads; settling fact: inline the witness half.) Runner-up, *disclosed*: `ok = (color_mode==0xf0 || color_mode==0x50) ? 0 : 1;` — defect persists for the other ten of twelve nibbles, now storing **uninitialized stack** bytes (the fills are deleted), a worse leak; `ycrcb put` stays green.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:20:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:21:## Q3 (REASONED)
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:22:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:23:Unnamed members: (1) **silent decline** — skip the store, never announce; met only as mutant M7, never priced as an option; (2) **store-unconverted / clamp-to-nearest-supported** — distinct mechanism from zero-fill, same rejection rationale, never named; (3) **exit-on-first-bad-pixel** — a fatal that actually exits; the loud alternative to latching; unnamed and rightly dead (guest-triggerable abort). Member 7 (IMPLEMENT YCRCB): refusal **still correct as far as this packet shows** — the constant 0xf0 is documented but no component layout is inlined, and a guessed packing silently publishes wrong colours, strictly worse than one loud decline. Settling fact: a CRMFB YCrCb layout spec; if one exists, member 7 reopens.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:24:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:25:## Q4
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:26:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:27:As PRETABLE enumerates (2×3×3×2 = **36**): **none** — every non-fix cell is reddened (stores→`ycrcb put`; latch removed→`once`; shared→`latch indep`; guard removed→`ycrcb put`; guard-inside→`two declined`; type dropped→its accept row; I spot-checked the masking combinations, e.g. {stores × guard-inside} still reddens `ycrcb put`). **But "shared" is one lattice value standing for twelve distinct programs.** Expanded per other-site (2×14×3×2 = 168), exactly **11 cells are dark** — {declines × shared-with-s_i × guard-kept × types-kept} for each site the sessions never fire — and no row's channel varies in them (walked all 14 for s = TEX_RD). "None" is true only of the 36-cell lattice as stated; the design's own sentence quantifies over "any other site," and under that quantifier there are 11 dark cells.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:28:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:29:## Q5
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:30:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:31:`live` ← M8_declineall (a drop-RGBA mutant would also do it — unplanned). `ci8 put` ← M9_dropcase_ci. `abgr put` ← M10_dropcase_abgr. **`rgb put` ← M8_declineall only** — the natural per-type growth mutant (drop `case DE_MODE_TYPE_RGB`) is missing from M1–M12, as is drop-RGBA for `live`. M8 reddens all four at once, so each row is falsifiable, but per-type growth attribution exists for only two of four accept rows. (M11_null cannot redden accept rows — they are green on HEAD by design.)
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:32:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:33:## Q6
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:34:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_glm.txt:35:Quote (hunk 1, enum comment): **"a latch shared with any other site is silenced by that site's ordinary traffic."** An observable consequence asserted under a universal quantifier; the only rows touching it (`once`, `latch indep`) vary under exactly one instantiation (BADMODE), and PRETABLE §2 has no sentence disclosing the other eleven sites — §3's "the disagreeing state the rule asks for … built in-session by `latch indep`" builds one site and, read as satisfying the rule, overstates. Same hole as Q2.
