regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:4:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:5:**(a)** (READ) In the shown PUT region the only MEM_WRITE is the now-guarded common tail; hunk 1 shows only `int ok = 1;` between `if (put) {` and the switch. GET byte-identical: (REASONED) yes, by diff mechanics — the else branch appears only as context lines, and anything outside a hunk is unchanged by definition of `git diff`. NOT SETTLEABLE: the RGB/RGBA/ABGR arm bodies between the two hunks are only partially inlined; a direct `memory_rw` inside an unshown arm would bypass `ok`. *Settles it:* the full text of the PUT switch arms.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:6:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:7:**(b)** (READ) After `ok = 0`, `buf` is referenced nowhere before the guarded store; the announce reads `color_mode, x, y`. NOT SETTLEABLE: any code after the else-block (function tail). PRETABLE asserts the store is "the only thing after the switch" — asserted, not shown. *Settles it:* the body from the else-block to the closing brace.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:8:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:9:**(c)** (READ) Enum tail shows `TEX_RD = 1<<11`, then `BADCOLOR = 1<<12` as last enumerator; the demotion narrative is internally consistent with the convention. NOT SETTLEABLE: non-enum writers of bit 12, occupancy of bits 0–3 (§3's "thirteen bits"), and the **width** of `d->warned`. Note: width < 13 bits is self-pinning (latch never sets → `once` reds); a collision with an unrowed site is not pinned. *Settles it:* `grep -n "warned" src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c` plus the struct definition.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:10:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:11:**(d)** (READ) The old literal is kept verbatim *as a prefix*, including its ` ]`, so substring greps survive. (REASONED) But the new line continues " `] sgi_re: …`", so any probe anchored on end-of-line after `]`, or any probe counting per-pixel occurrences (now once per process, by design), goes silent. NOT SETTLEABLE: whether such probes exist. *Settles it:* `grep -rn "color mode" regress/`.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:12:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:13:**(e)** ENUMERATED: `MODE_CI8 = 0x1000` → `(0x1000>>8)&3 = 0x10&3 = 0` → `bufdepth = 1<<0 = 1` byte (matches the `#100` comment's formula). `buf[0] = *color` truncates fg `0xaabbccdd` to `0xdd` at tile byte 0; under the detector's stated big-endian convention, byte 0 = top byte → `0xdd223344` ✓. The endianness itself is (REASONED) asserted by the packet and consistent with GXemul's ip32 being a big-endian MIPS machine, but not derived here. Cross-checks on fg `0xaabbccdd`: RGB `[R,G,B,0]` → `0xaabbcc00` ✓; ABGR byte-reversed → `0xddccbbaa` ✓.
