regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_kimi.txt:21:(REASONED) Two unnamed members. (i) Latch **granularity**: `once` quietly pins once-per-device-instance over once-per-nibble (under per-type latching `two declined` announces twice and reds) — a load-bearing choice never recorded as a decision. (ii) On member 7: YCRCB is per S1 a *documented* mode, so hardware has a defined behaviour; "refused for want of a packing spec" is an absence-of-spec premise I cannot check from this packet. Refusal is right **this round** (skip+announce is reversible and strictly better than PRNG; the announce is the mechanism that surfaces future demand) but member 7 should remain OPEN, not closed. Additionally: a guest-visible error/status member exists only if the RE has such a channel — not settleable here.
