regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:7:### Q1 — premises
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:8:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:9:**(a) Yes, and yes.** In the `if (put)` arm the only `memory_rw(..., MEM_WRITE ...)` is the one behind `if (ok)`. Named cases only fill `buf`. The GET arm is the `else` of `if (put)` and is not in the diff: it still does the unguarded READ, the four-case unpack, and the unlatched `fatal("[ get: color mode = 0x%x ]\n", color_mode)`. Byte-identical to the pre-fix GET as far as the two hunks show.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:10:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:11:**(b) No.** With `ok == 0` the WRITE is skipped and the function returns. Nothing in the PUT arm reads `buf` after the switch. (The GET arm is the other branch.)
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:12:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:13:**(c) Yes, it was free; it is now this bit.** Walked every `d->warned` user in `dev_sgi_re.c`. Bits in use: `1<<0` … `1<<11` (LEN ×6, DE_LEN, UNMAP_WR/RD, PRIM_OP, BADMODE, TEX_RD), then `SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12` at the two sites (test + `|=`). No other `1 << 12` on `warned`. The hits on `0x1000` are `relative_addr += 0x1000` / `baseaddr + 0x1000`, not the latch. `warned` is `uint32_t`. Next-free sentence now sits on this enumerator as `1 << 13`.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:14:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:15:**(d) No live probe or gate goes silent.** Grep of `regress/*.py` and `regress/*.sh` (not artifact copies) for `color mode =`: only this probe. It keys on the prefix substring `[ put: color mode = 0xf0 ]`, which the new `fatal` still emits. GET keeps the old spelling. Artifact clones of pre-fix `dev_sgi_re.c` are not live oracles.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:16:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:17:**(e) Yes, and yes — and the 14/14 log already measured it.** `MODE_CI8 = 0x1000` → `bufdepth = 1 << ((0x1000 >> 8) & 3) = 1`. CI stores `buf[0] = *color` → `0xdd`. LIN_A PUT at vertex (0,0) writes that one byte at tile offset 0. `machine_sgi.c` sets `EMUL_BIG_ENDIAN`, so a word load of paint `0x11223344` with byte 0 replaced is `0xdd223344`. `FIX519_detector_run1.out` has `ci8 put 0xdd223344 ok`.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:18:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:19:**Type-nibble domain (enumerated, not counted):** `color_mode = mode & 0xf0` produces exactly `{0x00,0x10,…,0xf0}` (16). Cases: CI `0x00`, RGB `0x10`, RGBA `0x20`, ABGR `0x30`. Default: the other 12, including documented `DE_MODE_TYPE_YCRCB = 0xf0`. `DEVICE_ACCESS` does not mask `de_reg`; a guest store can produce every nibble. Packet’s “twelve of sixteen” holds.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:20:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:21:Witness logs match the packet: HEAD `2/5` (`0x56e8857a` / `0x38abc4e1` on YCRCB), detector HEAD `6/14`, fix `14/14`. `fatal()` returns (`debugmsg.c`, no `exit`). No live `random()` call remains in this file (five hits, all comments).
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:22:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:23:---
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:24:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:25:### Q2 — smallest edit that still passes all 14
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:26:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:27:**`if (ok)` → `if (ok || x)`** (one extra disjunct). Every PUT in the probe is a 1×1 rectangle at vertex `(0,0)`, so `x == 0` and the guard still equals `ok`. A YCRCB PUT at `(1,0)` stores again (unassigned `buf` / the old PRNG shape if reinstated). **Every row stays green**, including `ycrcb put`. Same family: `if (ok || y)`, `if (ok || !linear)` (probe colour PUTs are LIN_A; tiled TLB_A is unrowed).
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:28:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:29:Second one-token form, different property: **`SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR` → `SGIRE_W_TEX_RD` (or any bit except BADMODE) in the test and the `|=`.** `latch indep` only pre-fires BADMODE via LIN_B (`MODE_LINB_RGBA = 0x1620` → `tlb_mode = 5` → `#504` return). Ordinary TEX/width traffic would then silence the colour announce; all 14 stay green.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:30:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:31:Third, announce-only: **`fatal` → `debug` on the new string.** This probe `step`s every store, so `debug()` prints (`single_step` raises `v`). Free-running, `debug()` is silent at default verbosity and the announce vanishes. All 14 still green.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:32:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:33:I did not build these (git denied; no gate/harness run). They are readings of the probe’s coordinates + the latch partner + `debug()` vs `fatal()` under `step`.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:34:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:35:---
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:36:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:37:### Q3 — option set
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:38:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:39:**Member 7 IMPLEMENT YCRCB is still refused, correctly.** `YCRCB` in `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` is the `crmfbreg.h` `#define` plus this comment. No packing, subsample, or byte-order anywhere in the helper or the DE/MTE callers. Eleven of the twelve default nibbles are unnamed. Implementing `0xf0` in the same round as declining the rest is two designs.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:40:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:41:Named here: **3** (chosen: skip store + own-bit latched announce), **zero-fill-and-store** (rejected; not 4 — 4 is “model already computes the right value”; this arm computed `random()`).
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:42:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:43:**Not named, and not available at this site:**
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:44:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:45:- **4 ACCEPT** — nothing correct is computed and then discarded.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:46:- **5 FAULT** — `horrible_getputpixel` is `void`; the WRITE uses `NO_EXCEPTIONS | PHYSICAL`. There is no bus-error return to `memory_rw` from a drawing-helper pixel. Same “check the member is available on this path” limit as Alpha FAULT.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:47:- **6 BACKED ACCEPT** — invent YCbCr storage. That is 7 without a spec.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:48:- **2 silent decline** — skip store, no announce. Distinct from 3; not argued.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:49:- **ALIAS to RGBA** — a packing guess. `ycrcb put` would go red (`0xaabbccdd` ≠ paint), so the rows catch it if someone ships it.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:50:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:51:No missing *available* member that should have displaced 3.
