regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:73:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:74:| row | growth mutant that reddens it | want → got |
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:75:|---|---|---|
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:76:| `live` (RGBA) | **drop the RGBA case** (not in the planned 12) or `ok = 0` before the switch (M8) | `0xaabbccdd` → paint `0x11223344` |
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:77:| `ci8 put` | **M9 drop CI** | `0xdd223344` → `0x11223344` |
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:78:| `rgb put` | **drop RGB** (not in the planned 12); M8 also reddens it, but it also reddens the other three accept rows | `0xaabbcc00` → paint |
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:79:| `abgr put` | **M10 drop ABGR** | `0xddccbbaa` → paint |
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:80:| `live silent` | **M_announceall** (announce on the accept path). **Not** the `ok = 0` initializer form of M8: that skips every store **without** hitting `default:`’s `fatal`, so `ANN` stays 0 and this row stays green while `live` goes red. PRETABLE’s pairing of `live silent` with M_declineall is form-dependent. |
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:81:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/grok.txt:82:Each of the four packing rows *is* failable under drop-that-case. Two of those mutants are missing from the table plan. `live silent` is failable only under an announce-on-accept mutant.
