regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:1:VERDICT: The brief's derivations are mostly sound. Two real defects. Several premises not checkable from the packet.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:2:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:3:**DEFECT 1 — PRETABLE §1 mis-attributes what `two declined` pins.** The brief states "the `two declined' row is what pins 'skipped' rather than 'returned early' for the second PUT." This is wrong. Walk the row:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:4:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:5:- Fix (`ok = 0` + `if (ok)` guard): second PUT sets `ok = 0`, guard skips `memory_rw`, destination = paint. Row expects paint. **Pass.**
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:6:- Early `return` placed AFTER the latch block (announce + latch still fire, then return): second PUT finds latch set, no announce, returns before the store, destination = paint. Row expects paint. **Pass.**
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:7:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:8:The two mutants are observationally indistinguishable on this row. `two declined` catches `M4_okinlatch` (where the second PUT's `ok` is left at 1 and the store runs with an unassigned `buf`), but it does NOT catch early return.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:9:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:10:**DEFECT 2 — Q2 falls out of Defect 1.** The smallest edit that violates the design's "never an early `return`: the common tail is that store" rule and still passes all 14 rows is to move `return;` to after the latch block in the default arm (and drop the now-dead `ok = 0;`). All 14 rows stay green. No row reddens. The PRETABLE's claim that `two declined` would redden it is the trap; it does not.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:11:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:12:---
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:13:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:14:**Q1 — premise audit, extensionally**
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:15:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:16:(a) `ok` gates the only store in the PUT branch, GET byte-identical: **TRUE, READ.** The diff's only `memory_rw(..., MEM_WRITE, ...)` is the one wrapped in `if (ok)`. The `else` arm (GET) is untouched in the hunk.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:17:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:18:(b) With `ok == 0`, is `buf` read before return: **TRUE, READ.** After the switch the only consumer of `buf` is the guarded `memory_rw(..., buf, bufdepth, ...)`. `fatal`'s arguments are `color_mode, x, y` — no `buf`.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:19:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:20:(c) Bit 12 free in `enum`: **NOT CHECKABLE.** The diff shows the enum up through `SGIRE_W_TEX_RD = 1 << 11` and adds `SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12`. I cannot grep `dev_sgi_re.c` for other writers to `d->warned & (1<<12)`. Single fact that would settle: a grep of `dev_sgi_re.c` for `(1 << 12)` / `0x1000` / `BIT(12)` returning no hits.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:21:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:22:(d) Keeping the old literal as a prefix: any regress probe keyed on the old per-pixel text now silent: **NOT CHECKABLE.** I cannot grep `regress/` for `color mode =`. Single fact: the grep result. (Note: the *frequency* drops from per-pixel to once-per-instance, so any probe that counted occurrences would change — but I have no list of such probes.)
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:23:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:24:(e) `ci8 put` wants `0xdd223344`, ip32 big-endian, 8-bpp stores one byte: **TRUE, READ.** Pre-paint `0x11223344` → byte0 = `0x11` (top byte, big-endian). `MODE_CI8 = 0x1000` ⇒ `bufdepth = 1<<0 = 1`. CI arm writes `buf[0] = *color = 0xdd` (low byte of `0xaabbccdd`). Store writes one byte over byte0. Result: `0xdd223344`. Matches.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:25:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:26:**Q2 — smallest edit, all 14 rows green:** early `return` after the latch block in the default arm (drop `ok = 0;`). The PRETABLE's nominated pinner (`two declined`) does NOT redden. **No row reddens.** This is a real coverage gap the PRETABLE mis-stated as closed.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:27:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:28:**Q3 — option-set completeness at this arm:** **NOT CHECKABLE.** The packet inlines only member 3 (candidates (a) zero-fill-and-store rejected, (b) skip-the-store chosen). Members 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7 are not inlined. The parenthetical "member 7 IMPLEMENT YCRCB was refused for want of a packing spec — is that still right?" cannot be answered without (i) the packing spec for YCRCB and (ii) the rest of the option set. Single fact that would settle: the full design ruling for members 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, plus the YCRCB packing the design would have implemented.
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:29:
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:30:**Q4 — the floor:** Walking the cells. `default stores` is the original broken behavior (the pre-fix file); it is caught by `ycrcb put` / `reserved put` / `indep paint` (word ≠ paint) and is orthogonal to the latch/guard sub-axes (which are no-ops there). `default declines` × {latch kept/removed/shared} × {guard kept/removed/inside-latch} × {types kept/one dropped}: every non-baseline cell is hit by at least one of `ycrcb put`, `reserved put`, `two declined`, `once`, `latch indep`, `indep paint`, `announce text`, `live silent`, `ci8 put`, `rgb put`, `abgr put`. **NONE, denominator 36** (or 24 if you exclude the impossible composites `{guard removed, inside-latch}` and the `default stores` × {guard removed, inside-latch} cells where the sub-axis is vacuous).
regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260910/ollama_minimax.txt:31:
