1:#!/usr/bin/env python3
2:#
3:#  sgirandomcolour -- RUNG-3 WITNESS for dev_sgi_re.c horrible_getputpixel() colour-mode default.
4:#
5:#  THE DEFECT.  horrible_getputpixel() extracts `color_mode = mode & DE_MODE_TYPE_MASK' (mask 0xf0)
6:#  and switches on it during a PUT.  Four cases are implemented:
7:#    case DE_MODE_TYPE_CI:   buf[0] = *color;
8:#    case DE_MODE_TYPE_RGB:  buf[0] = *color >> 24; buf[1] = *color >> 16; buf[2] = *color >> 8; buf[3] = 0;
9:#    case DE_MODE_TYPE_RGBA: buf[0] = *color >> 24; buf[1] = *color >> 16; buf[2] = *color >> 8; buf[3] = *color;
10:#    case DE_MODE_TYPE_ABGR: buf[0] = *color; buf[1] = *color >> 8; buf[2] = *color >> 16; buf[3] = *color >> 24;
11:#  The `default:' arm executes:
12:#    buf[0] = random(); buf[1] = random(); buf[2] = random(); buf[3] = random();
13:#    fatal("[ put: color mode = 0x%x ]\n", color_mode);
14:#  and then allows the common tail to execute:
15:#    cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, tileptr + ofs, buf, bufdepth, MEM_WRITE, NO_EXCEPTIONS | PHYSICAL);
16:#  which writes bufdepth bytes of that buffer to guest memory -- the four random() fills at 32 bpp, one
17:#  of them at 8 bpp, and at bufdepth 8 those four plus an uninitialised tail (sgirebufuninit).  fatal()
18:#  does not exit.
19:#
20:#  REACHABILITY: 12 of the 16 nibbles reach default:, including the documented DE_MODE_TYPE_YCRCB
21:#  (0x000000f0 per crmfbreg.h) and reserved encodings such as 0x50.
22:#
23:#  POST-FIX BEHAVIOUR: an unhandled / unimplemented colour mode during a PUT declines and skips
24:#  writing to memory, leaving the destination pre-paint intact.
25:#
26:#  CONTRACT (vacuity-floor clause (e)) -- what this witness catches and what it does NOT:
27:#    CATCHES   the default arm assigning random() and storing it: `ycrcb put' and `reserved put'
28:#              expect the destination to remain unchanged (post-fix honest decline); on HEAD they
29:#              fail because host random() bytes overwrite the pre-painted sentinel.
30:#    DOES NOT  implement YCRCB colour space conversion or other colour modes; it witnesses the defect
31:#              on unhandled modes under ordinary bounds-correctness engineering.
32:#
33:#  usage: sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py <gxemul-binary> [label]
