Likely constructible in #504's shape (`-E sgi -e ip32`, real dispatch, same script red/green): pre-seed, declined put, read back, post-op defined-mode control proving the device isn't wedged. The packet names `draw_primitive()` as a caller that writes to the destination (READ), so a PUT through this helper is plausibly driven the same way. The single blocking premise is UNSETTLED #2: if the register-write path masks mode bits to defined types or rejects the store upstream, **no witness exists**, the round is documented-only, and "12 of 16" then describes host-reachable states no real guest can reach. The readback channel's mechanism is likewise not shown; I rely on #504's witness having observed destination bytes, which the packet asserts.

