1:# `#519` sgirandomcolour — PASS 2 ON THE REAL DIFF: the colour-type PUT default wrote four host-PRNG bytes into guest memory; it now declines the store once-announced
2:
3:## READ THIS FIRST — PLEASE DO NOT SIMPLY RATIFY
4:
5:A recent panel had seven of nine seats confirm a premise this brief's author stated
6:wrongly.  **Check the premises, not just the derivations.**  Where I state something as
7:fact, ask whether it is true.  A seat that re-derives a premise from something this brief
8:did NOT give it is worth more than a seat that agrees.
9:
10:**THE TREE UNDER REVIEW IS `GXEMUL-SEC/src/`.**  There are THREE pristine-2021-upstream
11:copies of GXemul under the project root (`./src/` and two under
12:`_archive/audit-results-*/builds/`).  They are NOT this fork.  If your line numbers
13:disagree with mine by hundreds you are reading one of them — say so rather than
14:reconciling.
15:
16:**If you cannot read files that is expected** — every fact you need is inlined.  Name any
17:premise you cannot settle from this packet rather than guessing at it.
18:
19:**Where this brief states an ARITHMETIC claim — an index range, an offset, a count of
20:reachable addresses — ENUMERATE it rather than reasoning about it.**  Walk the values.
21:A derivation that skips one masking line reads exactly like a correct one.
22:
23:**And ENUMERATE THE RIGHT DOMAIN — a domain is itself a premise.**  Ask what the PRODUCER of
24:these values can actually emit before you walk them.  Walking every member of a set you have
25:not audited is not enumeration; it is a derivation with more steps, and it reads exactly like
26:
27:## §C0 — HAS THIS ROUND SHIPPED?  NO.
28:HEAD is `1ce8296`. The diff below is the UNCOMMITTED working set of `GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c`
29:(`git diff -- src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c`, 2 hunks, 58 changed lines) plus a NEW file
30:`regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py` (untracked; the witness half was built by the agy seat, the detector
31:half is inlined below). Ordinary bounds-correctness work on a drawing-engine pixel helper; plain language.
32:
33:## §C — SETTLED PREMISES, RE-INLINED (say which you cannot settle from this packet)
34:S1. THE DEFECT. `horrible_getputpixel()` in `dev_sgi_re.c`: the PUT branch switches on
35:    `color_mode = mode & DE_MODE_TYPE_MASK` (0xf0). Four cases (CI 0x00, RGB 0x10, RGBA 0x20, ABGR 0x30 --
36:    `crmfbreg.h:328-331`); the `default:` arm assigned `buf[0..3] = random()`, called an UNLATCHED per-pixel
37:    `fatal()` (which RETURNS: `debugmsg.c:384`, no exit), and fell through to the common
38:    `cpu->memory_rw(... buf, bufdepth, MEM_WRITE ...)`. Twelve of sixteen nibbles reach it, `DE_MODE_TYPE_YCRCB`
39:    (0xf0, documented) among them.
40:S2. WITNESS (rung 3, agy seat, unmodified `-E sgi -e ip32`, DE rectangle PUT through LIN_A at a physical tile,
41:    destination pre-painted 0x11223344, fg 0xaabbccdd): on HEAD `SGICOLOUR_RESULT=2/5` -- the YCRCB PUT read
42:    0x56e8857a (run 1) / 0x38abc4e1 (run 2), the reserved-type 0x50 PUT likewise, neither the paint nor any
43:    packing of the colour, different across runs because `main.c` seeds `random()` per process; attribution
44:    text `[ put: color mode = 0xf0 ]` present. On the fix, 5/5 with the same script; with the nine detector
45:    rows below, 14/14 on the fix and 6/14 on HEAD (`regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/witness_20260910/`,
46:    `fix_20260910/`).
47:S3. DESIGN (pass-1 panel 2026-09-08, five seats; codex DESIGN2 reading; flagship ruling 2026-09-09): option-set
48:    member 3, candidate (b) -- SKIP THE STORE for an unsupported type (a one-local `ok` guard around the single
49:    store, never an early `return`: the common tail is that store), delete the random() fills and the per-pixel
50:    fatal, announce ONCE per device instance on an INDEPENDENT latch bit. Rejected: (a) zero-fill-and-store
51:    (publishes a colour the guest never asked for). The GET default arm is a SEPARATE row (`sgirebufuninit`)
52:    and is untouched. The old literal `[ put: color mode = 0x%x ]` is kept as the announce's prefix because the
53:    witness attributes on it.
54:S4. THE LATCH: `SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12`, added as the LAST enumerator with the enum's own "next free bit"
55:    sentence moved to it and the previous holder's copy demoted (the convention every entry in that enum
56:    records). `SGIRE_W_BADMODE` (1 << 10) is the same function's TLB/mode-switch decline (`#504`) -- a different
57:    event with a different text.
58:S5. PRE-TABLE CHECK written before any table (`killtable_20260910/PRETABLE.out`, inlined at the end).
59:
60:## THE DIFF (src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c, verbatim)
