222:## THE PRE-TABLE CHECK (verbatim)
223:```
224:#519 sgirandomcolour -- PRE-TABLE CHECK, written 2026-09-10 ~04:2x BEFORE table 1 runs (mtime is the proof).
225:Instrument: regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py -- 5 witness rows (agy, 2/5 on HEAD 1ce8296, 5/5 on the
226:fix) + 9 detector rows appended by the main loop.  Diff under review: src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c
227:(scratchpad/patch_sgirc.py, 58 changed lines): SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12 as the last enumerator, an `ok'
228:local in the PUT branch, the default arm declining (ok = 0, once-latched announce keeping the old
229:`[ put: color mode = 0x%x ]' literal as its prefix), the store guarded by `if (ok)'.  Product code
230:otherwise untouched; the GET default arm is NOT in scope (sgirebufuninit).
231:
232:1. SIBLING PARITY
233:   The PUT default arm's sibling is the GET default arm in the same function (reads raw, announces
234:   per pixel, unlatched) -- NOT touched here; its row is sgirebufuninit and it is DISCLOSED in the
235:   contract.  The TLB/mode switch's default (SGIRE_W_BADMODE, #504) is the nearest de-fatalised
236:   sibling: latched, returns before any store.  Channels there: announce once, `*color' untouched.
237:   Channels here: announce once (its OWN bit -- `latch indep' rows the independence), destination
238:   untouched (`ycrcb put', `reserved put', `two declined', `indep paint').  ASYMMETRY: #504's arm
239:   RETURNS; this one falls through to the common tail with the store skipped -- deliberate (the
240:   sketch rule: the tail's memory_rw is the only thing after the switch, and it is what the guard
241:   skips), and the `two declined' row is what pins "skipped" rather than "returned early" for the
242:   second PUT.
243:2. CLAIM -> ROW
244:   "the STORE IS SKIPPED, so the destination keeps what the guest had"     -> ycrcb put, reserved put,
245:                                                                              two declined, indep paint
246:   "not a zero fill"                                                        -> ycrcb put (0 would red)
247:   "announce is latched on its own bit"                                     -> once, latch indep
248:   "the old literal is kept as the prefix: the witness attributes on it"   -> ycrcb attrib (unchanged),
249:                                                                              announce text
250:   "A declined PUT never reads buf"                                          -> no row: not observable
251:                                                                              (no store); SENTENCE.
252:   "Twelve of the sixteen type nibbles reach here"                          -> two driven (0xf0, 0x50);
253:                                                                              the arm does not read the
254:                                                                              value; SENTENCE (contract).
255:   "main.c seeds random() per process"                                      -> the witness's determinism
256:                                                                              row measured it; no fix row.
257:3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
258:   Guard: color_mode (a local from `mode').  Body: `ok', d->warned.  The shared field d->warned now
259:   has thirteen bits; the disagreeing state the rule asks for is another site's bit set first --
260:   built in-session by `latch indep' (SGIRE_W_BADMODE fired by a LIN_B PUT, then the colour decline).
261:   `ok' is a local written only by the default arm: its disagreeing state is "second declined PUT in
262:   the same process with the latch already set", built by `two declined'.
263:4. CHANNEL -- per row, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs
264:   ycrcb put / reserved put   (b) reinstatement (random fills + store); M_noguard (`if (ok)' removed:
265:                              stores an unassigned buf); M_zerofill (buf = 0, ok = 1)     -> word != paint
266:   two declined               M_okinlatch (`ok = 0' moved inside the latch condition)      -> word != paint
267:   once                       M_nolatch (latch guard removed)                              -> count 2
268:   latch indep                M_sharedbit (SGIRE_W_BADMODE used instead of BADCOLOR)       -> count 0
269:   indep paint                M_sharedbit does not vary this; (b) does (LIN_B returns; YCRCB stores) -> word
270:   announce text              (b) (old text only) ; M_silent (announce removed)             -> count 0
271:   live silent                M_declineall (ok = 0 for every type) ; M_announceall            -> count 1 / word
272:   ci8 / rgb / abgr put       M_dropcase_X (the case removed -> falls to default -> paint)  -> word
273:   VACUOUS-BY-CONSTRUCTION CHECK: `indep paint' is fixed under M_sharedbit (both PUTs skip their
274:   store either way) -- it is a CONTROL for `latch indep', named as such; every other row's channel
275:   varies under its named mutant.
276:5. THE (d) ENUMERATION FOR TABLE 1 (bounded to the diff's hunks):
277:   dominating predicates: `put' (unchanged), `switch (color_mode)' (each supported type its own
278:   case; the default is one cell), `if (ok)' (introduced), the latch test (introduced).  Cells:
279:   {default declines / stores} x {latch kept / removed / shared} x {store guard kept / removed /
280:   inside-latch} x {supported types kept / one dropped}.  Planned mutants, one edit each:
281:   M1_reinstate (b)   M2_noguard   M3_zerofill   M4_okinlatch   M5_nolatch   M6_sharedbit
282:   M7_silent          M8_declineall   M9_dropcase_ci   M10_dropcase_abgr   M11_null (the pre-fix
283:   file wholesale)    M12_announce_prefix_dropped (the old literal removed from the text: kills
284:   `ycrcb attrib' -- an L4-shaped mutant; recorded because the prefix is load-bearing for the witness)
285:   ACCEPT rows: live (RGBA), ci8 put, rgb put, abgr put; growth mutants M9/M10 (a case dropped) and
286:   M8 (everything declined).
287:```
