289:## THE QUESTIONS — VERDICT LINE FIRST, then answer extensionally
290:Q1. THE PREMISE AUDIT, as questions. (a) Does `ok` really gate the ONLY store in the PUT branch, and does the
291:    GET branch remain byte-identical? (b) With `ok == 0`, is `buf` read anywhere before the function returns?
292:    (c) Is 1 << 12 free in `enum` (no other user of bit 12 of `d->warned` anywhere in `dev_sgi_re.c`)?
293:    (d) Does keeping the old literal as a prefix leave any OTHER probe or gate that keyed on the old
294:    per-pixel text now silent (grep `regress/` for `color mode =`)? (e) `ci8 put` wants 0xdd223344: is the
295:    ip32 word read big-endian so byte 0 is the top byte, and does an 8 bpp PUT store exactly one byte?
