I'll verify the uncommitted `#519` diff against `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` rather than the packet, then answer Q1-Q6 from what the files actually do.Git is blocked from this seat, so I'll read `GXEMUL-SEC` files and greps next to check each premise against the tree.The enum and latch look as claimed; next I'll read the full PUT/GET helper, the probe, and the `color mode` greps that could go silent.The helper and probe match the packet so far; I'll now check endianness, BYTEMASK, the GET arm vs pre-fix, and whether any live probe still keys on the old per-pixel text.**VERDICT: NOT RATIFY the detector as complete; the product fix is sound.** Premises (a)-(e) hold on the tree. Q2 names two one-token edits that keep all 14 rows green. Fix those (or disclose them) before table 1; do not ship the 14-row contract as written.

Read from `GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c` (PUT default at the `ok = 0` arm, GET `else` immediately below, enum ending `SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12`), `crmfbreg.h` (`DE_MODE_TYPE_*`), `debugmsg.c` (`fatal` has no early-out), `machine_sgi.c` (`EMUL_BIG_ENDIAN`), `regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py`, `PRETABLE.out`, and the `fix_20260910` / `witness_20260910` logs. Line numbers match the working tree, not the 2021 `./src/`. Git was denied here; scores below are from those logs, not a re-run.

---

### Q1 - premises

**(a) Yes, and yes.** In the `if (put)` arm the only `memory_rw(..., MEM_WRITE ...)` is the one behind `if (ok)`. Named cases only fill `buf`. The GET arm is the `else` of `if (put)` and is not in the diff: it still does the unguarded READ, the four-case unpack, and the unlatched `fatal("[ get: color mode = 0x%x ]\n", color_mode)`. Byte-identical to the pre-fix GET as far as the two hunks show.

**(b) No.** With `ok == 0` the WRITE is skipped and the function returns. Nothing in the PUT arm reads `buf` after the switch. (The GET arm is the other branch.)

**(c) Yes, it was free; it is now this bit.** Walked every `d->warned` user in `dev_sgi_re.c`. Bits in use: `1<<0` . `1<<11` (LEN x6, DE_LEN, UNMAP_WR/RD, PRIM_OP, BADMODE, TEX_RD), then `SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR = 1 << 12` at the two sites (test + `|=`). No other `1 << 12` on `warned`. The hits on `0x1000` are `relative_addr += 0x1000` / `baseaddr + 0x1000`, not the latch. `warned` is `uint32_t`. Next-free sentence now sits on this enumerator as `1 << 13`.

**(d) No live probe or gate goes silent.** Grep of `regress/*.py` and `regress/*.sh` (not artifact copies) for `color mode =`: only this probe. It keys on the prefix substring `[ put: color mode = 0xf0 ]`, which the new `fatal` still emits. GET keeps the old spelling. Artifact clones of pre-fix `dev_sgi_re.c` are not live oracles.

**(e) Yes, and yes - and the 14/14 log already measured it.** `MODE_CI8 = 0x1000`  `bufdepth = 1 << ((0x1000 >> 8) & 3) = 1`. CI stores `buf[0] = *color`  `0xdd`. LIN_A PUT at vertex (0,0) writes that one byte at tile offset 0. `machine_sgi.c` sets `EMUL_BIG_ENDIAN`, so a word load of paint `0x11223344` with byte 0 replaced is `0xdd223344`. `FIX519_detector_run1.out` has `ci8 put 0xdd223344 ok`.

**Type-nibble domain (enumerated, not counted):** `color_mode = mode & 0xf0` produces exactly `{0x00,0x10,.,0xf0}` (16). Cases: CI `0x00`, RGB `0x10`, RGBA `0x20`, ABGR `0x30`. Default: the other 12, including documented `DE_MODE_TYPE_YCRCB = 0xf0`. `DEVICE_ACCESS` does not mask `de_reg`; a guest store can produce every nibble. Packet's "twelve of sixteen" holds.

Witness logs match the packet: HEAD `2/5` (`0x56e8857a` / `0x38abc4e1` on YCRCB), detector HEAD `6/14`, fix `14/14`. `fatal()` returns (`debugmsg.c`, no `exit`). No live `random()` call remains in this file (five hits, all comments).

---

### Q2 - smallest edit that still passes all 14

**`if (ok)`  `if (ok || x)`** (one extra disjunct). Every PUT in the probe is a 1x1 rectangle at vertex `(0,0)`, so `x == 0` and the guard still equals `ok`. A YCRCB PUT at `(1,0)` stores again (unassigned `buf` / the old PRNG shape if reinstated). **Every row stays green**, including `ycrcb put`. Same family: `if (ok || y)`, `if (ok || !linear)` (probe colour PUTs are LIN_A; tiled TLB_A is unrowed).

Second one-token form, different property: **`SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR`  `SGIRE_W_TEX_RD` (or any bit except BADMODE) in the test and the `|=`.** `latch indep` only pre-fires BADMODE via LIN_B (`MODE_LINB_RGBA = 0x1620`  `tlb_mode = 5`  `#504` return). Ordinary TEX/width traffic would then silence the colour announce; all 14 stay green.

Third, announce-only: **`fatal`  `debug` on the new string.** This probe `step`s every store, so `debug()` prints (`single_step` raises `v`). Free-running, `debug()` is silent at default verbosity and the announce vanishes. All 14 still green.

I did not build these (git denied; no gate/harness run). They are readings of the probe's coordinates + the latch partner + `debug()` vs `fatal()` under `step`.

---

### Q3 - option set

**Member 7 IMPLEMENT YCRCB is still refused, correctly.** `YCRCB` in `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` is the `crmfbreg.h` `#define` plus this comment. No packing, subsample, or byte-order anywhere in the helper or the DE/MTE callers. Eleven of the twelve default nibbles are unnamed. Implementing `0xf0` in the same round as declining the rest is two designs.

Named here: **3** (chosen: skip store + own-bit latched announce), **zero-fill-and-store** (rejected; not 4 - 4 is "model already computes the right value"; this arm computed `random()`).

**Not named, and not available at this site:**

- **4 ACCEPT** - nothing correct is computed and then discarded.
- **5 FAULT** - `horrible_getputpixel` is `void`; the WRITE uses `NO_EXCEPTIONS | PHYSICAL`. There is no bus-error return to `memory_rw` from a drawing-helper pixel. Same "check the member is available on this path" limit as Alpha FAULT.
- **6 BACKED ACCEPT** - invent YCbCr storage. That is 7 without a spec.
- **2 silent decline** - skip store, no announce. Distinct from 3; not argued.
- **ALIAS to RGBA** - a packing guess. `ycrcb put` would go red (`0xaabbccdd` ? paint), so the rows catch it if someone ships it.

No missing *available* member that should have displaced 3.

---

### Q4 - floor cells

Stated product: `{default declines, stores} x {latch kept, removed, shared} x {guard kept, removed, inside-latch} x {types kept, one dropped}` = **36**.

**Inside that product: none unrowed for a single-edit occupant** (denominator 36). `ycrcb put`/`reserved put` cover default-stores; `two declined` covers inside-latch; `once` covers latch-removed; `latch indep` covers shared-with-BADMODE; `live`/`ci8 put`/`rgb put`/`abgr put` cover one-type-dropped.


